---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SeriesNav from '../../../components/SeriesNav.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../../consts';
import { getInsightBySlug, buildArticleJsonLd } from '../../../data/insights';
import { getAdjacentParts } from '../../../data/series';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const post = getInsightBySlug('four-states-hold-half-the-red')!;
const articleJsonLd = buildArticleJsonLd(post, SITE.url);
const { series, current, prev, next } = getAdjacentParts('poshan-tracker', post.slug);
const linkedInUrl = current!.linkedInUrl;
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Four states hold half the red | Causewave"
  description={post.description}
  ogTitle="Four states hold half the red"
  ogDescription="Madhya Pradesh, Bihar, Jharkhand and Tripura hold 68 of 132 very-high-risk districts. Four states. Half the red."
  ogImage={post.ogImage}
  ogImageAlt="Nutrition programme desk with growth charts, India map, and a weighing scale"
  canonicalPath={post.path}
  activePage="insights"
  ogType="article"
  breadcrumbLabel={`Part 4: ${post.shortTitle}`}
  breadcrumbParent={[
    { name: 'Insights', path: 'insights/' },
    { name: 'The Poshan Tracker File', path: 'insights/poshan-tracker/' },
  ]}
  jsonLd={articleJsonLd}
>
  <main>
    <section class="bg-slate-900 text-white section">
      <div class="max-w-screen-2xl mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="max-w-3xl">
          <a href={`${base}insights/poshan-tracker/`} class="inline-flex items-center text-sm text-slate-400 hover:text-white transition-colors mb-6">
            ← The Poshan Tracker File
          </a>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
            <span class="text-xs font-medium text-teal-400 bg-teal-400/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-full">Part 4 of 5</span>
            <span class="text-xs text-slate-500">{post.dateLabel}</span>
          </div>
          <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">{post.title}</h1>
          <p class="mt-4 text-slate-300 text-lg">{post.excerpt}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="section max-w-screen-2xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <SeriesNav series={series!} current={current!} prev={prev} next={next} />
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6 text-lg">
          Last week: 634 districts improved, 94 got worse. Delhi ten of eleven up. Telangana twenty-six of thirty-three.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          <a href={`${base}insights/two-nutrition-numbers/`} class="text-sky-600 hover:underline">Part 1 → Two nutrition numbers</a>
          {' · '}
          <a href={`${base}insights/132-districts/`} class="text-sky-600 hover:underline">Part 2 → 132 districts</a>
          {' · '}
          <a href={`${base}insights/634-down-94-up/`} class="text-sky-600 hover:underline">Part 3 → 634 down. 94 up.</a>
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          This week: forget the slope. Who holds the list now.
        </p>

        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          August 2026. Same 132 very-high-risk districts as
          <a href={`${base}insights/132-districts/`} class="text-sky-600 hover:underline">Part 2</a>.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Madhya Pradesh, Bihar, Jharkhand, Tripura:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-slate-600 mb-6">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-teal-500 mt-2 shrink-0"></span><span>125 districts of 787 in the file. Sixteen percent of India-on-the-dashboard.</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-teal-500 mt-2 shrink-0"></span><span>68 of 132 very-high-risk names. Fifty-two percent.</span></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          They are not “a few tribal blocks.” They are the pile.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-4">The four</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Madhya Pradesh. 55 districts. 38 very high risk. 16 high. 54 of 55 high or very high. Average score 22.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          That is 29% of all very-high-risk India, in one state. More than Bihar, Jharkhand and Gujarat put together.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Tripura. Eight districts. Six very high. Two high. Eight of eight. A small state can be 100% of itself and vanish inside a national average.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Jharkhand. 24 districts. 12 very high. 11 high. 96% of the state in the two top bands. West Singhbhum still the worst named row in the country.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          Bihar. 38 districts. 12 very high. 23 high. 92% high or very high.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-4">The floor</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Tamil Nadu. 38 districts. Zero high. Zero very high. Average 4.4.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Punjab, Haryana, Himachal, J&amp;K, Goa, Sikkim, Andaman, Ladakh, Chandigarh: the same empty column.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          The dashboard knows how to record a low-burden state. So 98% high-or-very-high in Madhya Pradesh is not “the app paints everything red.”
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          Do not convert Tamil Nadu’s 4.4 into an NFHS 4%.
          <a href={`${base}insights/two-nutrition-numbers/`} class="text-sky-600 hover:underline">Part 1</a>:
          prevalence is the survey. This is what the machine wrote. The contrast is still the point: the file can be quiet, and it can be a siren, in the same month.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-4">A falling average does not empty the pile</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Madhya Pradesh’s district score fell about eight points since 2023. Bihar six. Jharkhand two. They improved. They still are last week’s map.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Gujarat fell fifteen points and has two names on the 132. Telangana rose and has six.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          A note that “India is improving on Poshan Tracker” can be true in
          <a href={`${base}insights/634-down-94-up/`} class="text-sky-600 hover:underline">Part 3</a>
          and fail this part.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          The operational question is not a national vibe. It is: in the month the site calls current, are 38 districts in Madhya Pradesh still in the band we named very high risk? Yes.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-10 mb-4">This week’s only job</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Count. Four states. Half the red.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Not a claim that children in Tamil Nadu are fine. The survey still exists. Not a Burhanpur essay. The count that essay could not make.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-8">
          Next —{' '}
          <a href={`${base}insights/wasting-has-no-season/`} class="text-sky-600 hover:underline">
            Part 5: Wasting has no season
          </a>
          . Last of the national run: the indicator that should keep a season. The one the survey still puts near 19%, and the dashboard near 3%.
        </p>

        <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mb-8">
          <strong>Data:</strong> Part 4 of 5. Poshan Tracker, August 2026. Very high risk as in Part 2. Gujarat’s district count in the raw dashboard includes an empty id; it does not change the four-state arithmetic.
          Also on{' '}
          <a href={linkedInUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sky-600 hover:underline">LinkedIn</a>.
        </p>

        <SeriesNav series={series!} current={current!} prev={prev} next={next} />

        <div class="mt-8 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 border">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg">Designing healthcare and nutrition CSR that matches the map?</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
            Causewave helps companies with programme design and last-mile public health delivery.
            Explore <a href={`${base}services/`} class="text-sky-600 hover:underline">services</a> or get in touch.
          </p>
          <a href={`${base}contact/`} class="mt-4 inline-flex btn btn-primary px-6 py-2 text-sm">Get in Touch</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
